From: Chaos Ruler <zmelumian@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Thor DT: the UFS PHY's QREF buffer supply (with 9048, Kettle 1402)

The UFS PHY's reference clock runs through a QREF buffer on LDO L1E. Without a
vdda-qref consumer L1E sat in LPM with the screen off, and a wake from s2idle could
fail UFS PHY calibration (Kettle, Portal and Thor). 9048 gives the supply its 30 mA load.
---
--- a/projects/ROCKNIX/devices/SM8550/linux/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts
+++ b/projects/ROCKNIX/devices/SM8550/linux/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts
@@ -551,5 +551,9 @@
 &vreg_l3e_1p2 {
 	regulator-state-mem {
 		regulator-off-in-suspend;
 	};
 };
+
+&ufs_mem_phy {
+	vdda-qref-supply = <&vreg_l1e_0p88>;
+};
